
/*==============================================================================
  PRECAST WEB -> ORACLE EBS -> JOB COST
  UNIVERSAL TROUBLESHOOTING / RECONCILIATION SCRIPT
  Version: 2.2
  Built from confirmed table/view structures supplied 28-AUG-2026
  Corrected globally for Oracle NULL/blank SQL*Plus DEFINE handling

  PURPOSE
  -------
  This script is a SAFE, DIAGNOSTIC-FIRST runbook for almost any:
      - Precast Web vs Oracle Production variance
      - Oracle Production vs Job Cost variance
      - Missing production
      - Transfer mismatch
      - Reject / adjustment issue
      - Missing OP batch / outbound / Oracle lot
      - Duplicate lot / duplicate billing
      - Overage / short production
      - PA interface / Cost Distribution issue

  IMPORTANT ORACLE PARAMETER RULE
  -------------------------------
  Oracle treats an empty string ('') as NULL.
  Therefore optional input predicates MUST use:

      '&&P_PARAMETER' IS NULL OR column = ...

  Do NOT use:

      '&&P_PARAMETER' IS NULL OR column = ...

  BAD / DO NOT USE:
      '&&P_PARAMETER' = '' OR column = ...

  Oracle converts '' to NULL. NULL = NULL is not TRUE, so the BAD form can
  silently remove every row when an optional parameter is blank.

  GOLDEN RULE
  -----------
  DO NOT FIX DATA UNTIL THE FIRST WRONG STAGE IS PROVEN.

  DATA FLOW
  ---------
  PRECAST WEB
      PREC_PCF / PREC_PCF_PANELS
          ->
      PREC_TRANS_HEADER / PREC_TRANSACTIONS
          ->
      PREC_BATCHES / PREC_BATCH_HEADERS / PREC_BATCH_TRANSACTIONS
          ->
      WEB_RE_OUTBOUND_LOTS / WEB_RE_OUTBOUND_PROD
          ->
  ORACLE EBS
      RECO_LOT_NUMBERS
          ->
      RECO_PRODUCTION / RECO_PRODUCTION_V
          ->
      RECO_LB_PROD_BILLING / RECO_FLORIDA_PROD_BILLING
          ->
      RECO_PRECAST_LINKAGE
          ->
      PA_TRANSACTION_INTERFACE_ALL
          ->
      PA_EXPENDITURE_ITEMS_ALL / RECO_PRECAST_EXPENDITURES
          ->
      COST DISTRIBUTION / JOB COST

  THREE NUMBERS TO ALWAYS ESTABLISH
  ---------------------------------
      A. Precast Web physical production
      B. Oracle physical production
      C. Oracle Projects / Job Cost production

  IMPORTANT CONFIRMED STRUCTURE NOTES
  -----------------------------------
  1. RECO.RECO_PCF_V uses PROJECT_NUM (not PROJECT_NUMBER).
  2. PRODUCT_CODE is NOT in RECO.RECO_PCF_V.
     It is available in PREC_PCF@RECOWEBPROD.
  3. RECO.RECO_PRODUCTION does NOT contain PCF_ID / MARK_NUMBER / AREA.
  4. RECO.RECO_PRODUCTION_V DOES contain PCF_ID / MARK_NUMBER / AREA_PER_PIECE.
  5. RECO.RECO_PRODUCTION_V does NOT contain REVISION_NUMBER.
  6. RECO.RECO_LOT_NUMBERS does NOT contain REVISION_NUMBER.
  7. RECO_PRECAST_EXPENDITURES is a useful PA/Job Cost view:
       TASK_NUMBER, EXPENDITURE_TYPE, EXPENDITURE_ITEM_DATE, QUANTITY,
       PCF_ID, REVISION, TNUM, TASK_ID, PROJECT_ID, DENOM_RAW_COST.
  8. PRECAST Web header does NOT contain PCF_ID.
     PCF_ID is on PREC_TRANSACTIONS.
==============================================================================*/

